{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1319633-question-about-a-possible-mythological-scion-of-huehuecoyotl","id":1319633,"title":"Question about a possible mythological Scion of Huehuecoyotl","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-19T22:37:11-07:00","id":1319633,"title":"Question about a possible mythological Scion of Huehuecoyotl","content":"I had a friend ask me about a story they'd read somewhere about what sounds like a possible mythological chosen Scion of Huehuecoyotl. In the story they'd read, the Scion was originally a human woman who Huehuecoyotl became interested in romantically. He replaced her heart with copal, causing her to become immortal, and ultimately become a legendary wandering spirit figure, not too different from someone like La Llorona, but not malevolent. My friend said she was known as the &quot;Borderwalker,&quot; which is presumably an English translation of her Nahuatl name. I'm curious, given that she sounds like a possible chosen Scion. I haven't been able to find any reliable sources describing this story, however. If anyone on here knows anything, I'd love to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T01:33:10-07:00","id":1319661,"title":"","content":"This appears to be from a TV show:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://supernatural.fandom.com/wiki/Borderwalker\" target=\"_blank\">https://supernatural.fandom.com/wiki/Borderwalker</a><br /> <br /> Although maybe the show's writers used genuine folkloric sources as inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-